            "text": "2FA bypass / totpSecret leakage — No issue identified: POST /rest/2fa/* (status, setup, verify, disable)\n\nFull 2FA lifecycle tested: setup requires password, verify requires tmpToken+valid TOTP. Code replay with the SAME tmpToken is accepted (no one-time-use enforcement) but fresh tmpTokens cannot reuse an old code and the accepted time window is narrow (rejected 1 window old codes in brute test) — practically not exploitable. 2FA disable requires password. Status endpoint leaks own totpSecret+setupToken to the owner only (requires valid token). No cross-user secret read found; no bypass confirmed."
